1
00:00:10,031 --> 00:00:11,115
Have a nice trip.

2
00:00:33,638 --> 00:00:35,056
CUSTOMS OFFICIAL (MINISTRY OF FINANCE)
MACHI MORI

3
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:37,976
Well then, that wraps up our duties
for today! Great work, everyone!

4
00:00:38,059 --> 00:00:40,019
-Good work.
-Good work.

5
00:00:44,983 --> 00:00:47,026
Excuse me, Matsuyama.

6
00:00:48,152 --> 00:00:51,739
You didn't check that last passenger's
luggage. Was that okay?

7
00:00:52,323 --> 00:00:55,910
Oh. Well, nothing seemed
particularly suspicious.

8
00:00:56,786 --> 00:00:59,914
-But…
-You Customs folks take it easy, huh?

9
00:01:00,665 --> 00:01:01,833
I've been thinking about this for a while.

10
00:01:01,916 --> 00:01:04,752
You don't check everyone's baggage, right?

11
00:01:04,836 --> 00:01:06,212
Is that acceptable?

12
00:01:06,296 --> 00:01:08,965
True. Are you sure you're not
letting something slip by?

13
00:01:09,048 --> 00:01:12,719
We must always stay focused and observe
carefully, so it doesn't happen.

14
00:01:12,802 --> 00:01:17,015
And when a bag catches our eye,
we examine it thoroughly.

15
00:01:17,098 --> 00:01:19,559
We stop suspicious people every day.

16
00:01:19,642 --> 00:01:23,354
Exactly. At Customs,
every single second is a battle.

17
00:01:24,439 --> 00:01:25,815
It's not like Immigration,

18
00:01:25,899 --> 00:01:27,942
where you just chat
mindlessly with passengers.

19
00:01:28,026 --> 00:01:31,613
-Chat mindlessly?
-Immigration is so carefree. Sounds nice.

20
00:01:31,696 --> 00:01:33,948
-Could you please not lump us together?
-That's my line.

21
00:01:34,032 --> 00:01:37,619
Well, you know… Anyway, Mori,
was there something about

22
00:01:37,702 --> 00:01:40,079
that last passenger's luggage
that caught your attention?

23
00:01:40,163 --> 00:01:41,497
Yes, very much so.

24
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:43,750
What was it? Was something wrong?

25
00:01:44,375 --> 00:01:46,753
What are we going to do?
She's already gone through.

26
00:01:48,087 --> 00:01:50,048
The pattern on the front of her bag

27
00:01:52,133 --> 00:01:55,845
was Matyo embroidery.

28
00:01:57,096 --> 00:01:58,264
Matyo embroidery?

29
00:02:00,558 --> 00:02:02,810
It's traditional Hungarian embroidery.

30
00:02:02,894 --> 00:02:08,358
It features rounded rose petals
and a striking, vibrant red.

31
00:02:08,441 --> 00:02:11,611
It makes the flowers look almost alive.

32
00:02:12,195 --> 00:02:15,365
-Those are roses?
-It certainly is unique.

33
00:02:16,366 --> 00:02:18,409
And? What was suspicious about it?

34
00:02:18,493 --> 00:02:20,078
Oh, nothing in particular.

35
00:02:20,662 --> 00:02:23,623
But I just wanted
to inspect it more closely.

36
00:02:25,041 --> 00:02:27,126
What is wrong with this person?

37
00:02:32,882 --> 00:02:35,176
Yes, this is Gate 24.

38
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:39,681
Customs sure has it tough,
having to appraise embroidery too.

39
00:02:39,764 --> 00:02:41,224
Yes.

40
00:02:41,307 --> 00:02:44,060
Well, anyway, at least today
ended without incident.

41
00:02:44,143 --> 00:02:45,687
Um, um…

42
00:02:48,106 --> 00:02:50,358
T-There's a bomb threat.

43
00:02:51,693 --> 00:02:52,568
It seems.

44
00:02:53,736 --> 00:02:54,737
-What?
-What?

45
00:02:56,656 --> 00:02:58,491
Thank you. Keep us updated.

46
00:03:01,077 --> 00:03:02,453
Airport Director Ikeura.

47
00:03:04,247 --> 00:03:05,748
We just received this phone call.

48
00:03:07,792 --> 00:03:10,670
<i>This is the Kanto International</i>
<i>Airport Information Center.</i>

49
00:03:10,753 --> 00:03:13,965
<i>A bomb has been planted on the flight</i>
<i>bound for Rome International Airport.</i>

50
00:03:14,757 --> 00:03:17,635
-<i>Who is this?</i>
-<i>If you want it disarmed,</i>

51
00:03:17,719 --> 00:03:21,139
<i>prepare three million dollars</i>
<i>by midnight tonight.</i>

52
00:03:21,222 --> 00:03:23,683
<i>I repeat, a bomb has been planted</i>
<i>on the flight bound</i>

53
00:03:23,766 --> 00:03:25,643
<i>for Rome International Airport.</i>

54
00:03:26,561 --> 00:03:29,647
It could be a prank,
but we can't afford to ignore it.

55
00:03:29,731 --> 00:03:31,274
We are currently coordinating

56
00:03:31,357 --> 00:03:33,317
with security companies and the police.

57
00:03:34,694 --> 00:03:39,198
Bound for Rome…
Today, the only flight is EUW301.

58
00:03:39,282 --> 00:03:41,534
Yes. The flight cannot take off

59
00:03:41,617 --> 00:03:42,827
until safety checks are done.

60
00:03:43,453 --> 00:03:44,662
The passengers on this flight

61
00:03:44,746 --> 00:03:47,123
will need to be rebooked
on flights tomorrow or later.

62
00:03:47,206 --> 00:03:50,418
Then we will handle
those passengers at Gate 24.

63
00:03:50,501 --> 00:03:52,670
No, no, we'll handle them
at the main booth.

64
00:03:53,254 --> 00:03:55,381
In an emergency like this,
we'll have a backup booth--

65
00:03:55,465 --> 00:03:58,217
We will handle them.

66
00:03:59,677 --> 00:04:00,553
Okay.

67
00:04:09,354 --> 00:04:10,188
TIME TILL DETONATION: 4 HOURS

68
00:04:10,271 --> 00:04:14,567
Due to a bomb threat, Flight EUW301
has been canceled for today.

69
00:04:15,818 --> 00:04:18,404
The 23 transit passengers
scheduled for this flight

70
00:04:18,488 --> 00:04:20,656
will temporarily enter Japan.

71
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:24,327
These 23 individuals
are subject to strict inspection.

72
00:04:24,410 --> 00:04:26,537
We're handling that?

73
00:04:26,621 --> 00:04:29,165
So this time, we need
to inspect everyone's luggage.

74
00:04:30,041 --> 00:04:32,001
We need to check thoroughly
for explosives.

75
00:04:32,085 --> 00:04:34,253
Swiftly and carefully, right?

76
00:04:34,337 --> 00:04:35,588
Precisely.

77
00:04:36,339 --> 00:04:39,509
To avoid panic, we haven't informed
the passengers about the bomb threat,

78
00:04:39,592 --> 00:04:42,261
and flights other than this one
are operating as normal.

79
00:04:42,345 --> 00:04:45,264
What if a bomb is found?

80
00:04:45,348 --> 00:04:47,725
At that point,
all flights might be canceled.

81
00:04:47,809 --> 00:04:50,520
Prepare for every possible scenario.

82
00:04:50,603 --> 00:04:53,189
I'm heading
to the Crisis Management Center now.

83
00:04:58,736 --> 00:05:00,113
Don't panic.

84
00:05:00,196 --> 00:05:01,864
What you need
to do is the same as always.

85
00:05:02,448 --> 00:05:05,034
Pass who should pass,
and stop who should be stopped.

86
00:05:05,868 --> 00:05:07,787
And objects, too.

87
00:05:10,206 --> 00:05:11,666
Pass the objects that should pass,

88
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:14,627
and stop the objects
that should be stopped.

89
00:05:14,710 --> 00:05:16,003
Exactly.

90
00:05:17,130 --> 00:05:18,673
Make sure to carefully evaluate

91
00:05:20,133 --> 00:05:21,843
both people and objects.

92
00:05:21,926 --> 00:05:22,760
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

93
00:05:22,844 --> 00:05:24,303
All right, let's go, go, go.

94
00:05:26,222 --> 00:05:28,391
FLIGHT CANCELED

95
00:05:32,353 --> 00:05:33,896
Ah, Machi!

96
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:35,481
-Chika.
-We'll talk later.

97
00:05:35,565 --> 00:05:37,483
I brought the passengers.

98
00:05:52,915 --> 00:05:54,417
This is a problem.

99
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:57,170
I have an important
business meeting tomorrow.

100
00:05:57,253 --> 00:05:58,963
If I don't fly tonight, I won't make it.

101
00:05:59,589 --> 00:06:01,841
We are truly sorry for the inconvenience.

102
00:06:01,924 --> 00:06:04,093
What are you going to do
if my deal falls through?

103
00:06:04,177 --> 00:06:05,469
You'll owe me damages!

104
00:06:05,553 --> 00:06:08,264
We will arrange
for a later departure date.

105
00:06:08,347 --> 00:06:11,601
Why are we even being brought
all the way out here in the first place?

106
00:06:11,684 --> 00:06:12,810
Where are we?

107
00:06:12,894 --> 00:06:14,478
Man…

108
00:06:14,562 --> 00:06:15,980
This never happened to me before!

109
00:06:16,063 --> 00:06:16,981
Shall we go help?

110
00:06:19,192 --> 00:06:20,276
Enough with the apologies…

111
00:06:22,153 --> 00:06:22,987
‎What?

112
00:06:24,488 --> 00:06:26,782
Handling complaints
isn't in my jurisdiction.

113
00:06:27,992 --> 00:06:30,578
That might be true, but…

114
00:06:30,661 --> 00:06:31,871
What is this place?

115
00:06:32,914 --> 00:06:34,040
When are we going to fly?

116
00:06:37,251 --> 00:06:38,794
What's wrong with you?

117
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:46,219
-How many hours are we gonna wait?
-Are you hurt?

118
00:06:48,638 --> 00:06:50,097
‎We are still confriming...

119
00:06:50,181 --> 00:06:53,226
Please calm down.
Getting angry won't help anything.

120
00:06:53,309 --> 00:06:54,143
Huh?

121
00:06:54,227 --> 00:06:56,604
My whole life depends on this flight!

122
00:06:56,687 --> 00:06:59,148
-You're not the only one in a tough spot.
-Here you go.

123
00:06:59,232 --> 00:07:00,149
-Thank you.
-They are doing

124
00:07:00,233 --> 00:07:01,567
their best to handle the situation!

125
00:07:01,651 --> 00:07:03,653
So what? I'm a customer here!

126
00:07:03,736 --> 00:07:05,071
I'm a customer too.

127
00:07:05,154 --> 00:07:08,324
So is everyone else here.
So is this couple.

128
00:07:08,407 --> 00:07:10,409
All these passengers
are having trouble right now.

129
00:07:10,493 --> 00:07:13,162
Because of you, no one can hear
the explanations or get their luggage.

130
00:07:30,471 --> 00:07:31,973
-Thank you very much.
-It's okay.

131
00:07:53,286 --> 00:07:54,662
TOKYO METROPOLITAN POLICE

132
00:07:54,745 --> 00:07:56,330
-Call in.
-Roger.

133
00:07:59,458 --> 00:08:02,378
First floor passageway, all clear.

134
00:08:02,461 --> 00:08:04,797
Roger, please continue to search.

135
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:07,425
<i>Please look into this one more time.</i>

136
00:08:07,508 --> 00:08:08,676
<i>Nothing abnormal at the moment.</i>

137
00:08:08,759 --> 00:08:10,052
<i>Currently checking.</i>

138
00:08:10,136 --> 00:08:12,430
-Excuse me.
-Hello.

139
00:08:13,097 --> 00:08:14,056
‎I'm from Section 1, MPD.

140
00:08:14,432 --> 00:08:15,474
So?

141
00:08:53,095 --> 00:08:57,266
But I hurt my leg right before we left.

142
00:08:57,350 --> 00:09:00,936
Oh, that's unfortunate.
Please, don't force yourself.

143
00:09:06,484 --> 00:09:07,818
What is this?

144
00:09:07,902 --> 00:09:10,738
It's my husband's. He loves crafting.

145
00:09:10,821 --> 00:09:15,242
Oh my… By any chance,
did he craft that pendant as well?

146
00:09:15,826 --> 00:09:17,328
Oh, yes.

147
00:09:19,413 --> 00:09:22,166
It's lovely. That pretty lady
in the photograph…

148
00:09:22,249 --> 00:09:23,876
Is she your daughter?

149
00:09:23,959 --> 00:09:25,336
Yes, that's Emma.

150
00:09:29,215 --> 00:09:34,095
Our only child. She's been
performing in Norway these days.

151
00:09:34,178 --> 00:09:37,473
-Amazing! She's a professional violinist.
-Yes.

152
00:09:42,311 --> 00:09:44,563
-Natori, could you take over for a moment?
-Yes.

153
00:09:45,272 --> 00:09:46,357
Just a moment, please.

154
00:09:51,862 --> 00:09:53,030
The police?

155
00:09:53,698 --> 00:09:55,241
Hello. Is something the matter?

156
00:09:55,324 --> 00:09:57,034
No, just a quick check.

157
00:09:57,118 --> 00:09:58,369
Please don't mind us.

158
00:09:58,452 --> 00:10:00,579
The bomb threat, right?
Do you have information on the suspect--

159
00:10:00,663 --> 00:10:02,790
I told you, don't worry about it.

160
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:12,967
-Everything all right?
-Yes.

161
00:10:13,050 --> 00:10:14,719
How about the luggage?

162
00:10:14,802 --> 00:10:17,555
-No issues--
-Um…

163
00:10:17,638 --> 00:10:19,223
About this…

164
00:10:19,974 --> 00:10:23,394
Mori, I know you like things
like embroidery, but not here!

165
00:10:24,729 --> 00:10:25,813
Everything is fine.

166
00:10:27,690 --> 00:10:29,483
Please, go ahead.

167
00:10:30,109 --> 00:10:31,026
Here you are.

168
00:10:33,237 --> 00:10:34,071
‎Thank you.

169
00:10:35,114 --> 00:10:36,323
Take care.

170
00:10:44,457 --> 00:10:45,541
All right.

171
00:10:48,419 --> 00:10:50,004
What did the police want?

172
00:10:50,087 --> 00:10:52,131
They wouldn't tell me anything.

173
00:10:52,214 --> 00:10:54,008
What? What's that about?

174
00:10:54,091 --> 00:10:57,845
Again? Times like this are when
we should be sharing information.

175
00:10:58,512 --> 00:10:59,847
Next, please.

176
00:10:59,930 --> 00:11:01,682
-Passport, please.
-Yes.

177
00:11:06,353 --> 00:11:07,396
Your luggage, please.

178
00:11:08,022 --> 00:11:09,607
May I check your luggage?

179
00:11:12,276 --> 00:11:13,235
Go ahead.

180
00:11:14,737 --> 00:11:17,990
I'm only staying in Japan overnight,
but I'm still getting checked, huh?

181
00:11:18,073 --> 00:11:19,992
My apologies. This is a security check.

182
00:11:20,075 --> 00:11:21,494
LEFT FINGERPRINT
RIGHT FINGERPRINT

183
00:11:24,997 --> 00:11:25,998
Could you come here?

184
00:11:26,749 --> 00:11:27,791
‎Yes.

185
00:11:27,875 --> 00:11:30,503
-Sakura Nakae, right?
-Yes.

186
00:11:30,586 --> 00:11:33,088
You currently reside
in the Republic of Lorishika.

187
00:11:34,173 --> 00:11:35,341
What is your occupation?

188
00:11:35,424 --> 00:11:37,593
I teach at a Japanese language school.

189
00:11:37,676 --> 00:11:40,304
-How long have you been there?
-About three years.

190
00:11:41,055 --> 00:11:43,307
Before that, I taught
in a few other countries.

191
00:11:44,683 --> 00:11:45,893
Is there a problem?

192
00:11:47,478 --> 00:11:48,687
Please wait a moment.

193
00:11:48,771 --> 00:11:50,189
SAKURA NAKAE

194
00:12:00,199 --> 00:12:01,033
DUST-FREE CHALK

195
00:12:01,116 --> 00:12:03,452
Thank you for waiting.
The luggage is all clear?

196
00:12:04,537 --> 00:12:05,871
Oh, yes.

197
00:12:06,956 --> 00:12:07,915
KANTO 26/6/2009

198
00:12:07,998 --> 00:12:09,625
Here you are.

199
00:12:11,252 --> 00:12:12,086
May I?

200
00:12:12,169 --> 00:12:13,629
-Yes, there's no problem.
-Okay.

201
00:12:15,589 --> 00:12:18,717
What was that about just now?
You were looking something up.

202
00:12:21,095 --> 00:12:24,139
I can't tell you.
That's Immigration information.

203
00:12:24,223 --> 00:12:27,017
Hey, didn't we decide earlier

204
00:12:27,101 --> 00:12:29,770
that we should share
information within the team?

205
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:33,357
I decide what gets shared from here.

206
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:36,527
Now, now, as long as there
wasn't a problem, it's okay, right?

207
00:12:36,610 --> 00:12:39,488
-We've safely sent off all the passengers.
-Right.

208
00:12:39,572 --> 00:12:41,574
No, there's still one person left.

209
00:12:41,657 --> 00:12:42,491
-What?
-What?

210
00:12:44,493 --> 00:12:45,786
That one…

211
00:13:02,595 --> 00:13:05,222
Excuse me. Please step up for processing.

212
00:13:05,306 --> 00:13:07,391
-No, I'm fine.
-Pardon?

213
00:13:08,058 --> 00:13:10,769
Even if I get out of here,
I'm flying tomorrow anyway, right?

214
00:13:10,853 --> 00:13:13,022
Going back and forth is a waste of effort.

215
00:13:13,647 --> 00:13:16,358
I'll just spend the night here.

216
00:13:17,443 --> 00:13:20,279
I have no intention
of going through immigration.

217
00:13:24,867 --> 00:13:26,285
Oh my…

218
00:13:26,368 --> 00:13:27,828
<i>Please continue your search.</i>

219
00:13:27,911 --> 00:13:29,830
-<i>I'll confirm from here.</i>
-<i>No issues found.</i>

220
00:13:30,372 --> 00:13:33,000
So far, no suspicious objects
have been found.

221
00:13:33,083 --> 00:13:37,212
The caller said to prepare three million
dollars by midnight, correct?

222
00:13:37,296 --> 00:13:41,550
Yes. Still, preparing that
much cash in this timeframe…

223
00:13:42,217 --> 00:13:44,303
Counselor, can't you do
something about it?

224
00:13:44,928 --> 00:13:47,890
If I had such convenient authority,
I would have used it already.

225
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:50,893
How does the culprit

226
00:13:51,685 --> 00:13:54,355
plan to receive the money?

227
00:13:54,438 --> 00:13:55,856
Who knows?

228
00:13:55,939 --> 00:13:58,317
There's been no further contact.

229
00:13:59,068 --> 00:14:03,113
Excuse me, sir. This is a restricted area.

230
00:14:03,197 --> 00:14:05,532
In any case,
we can't have you staying here.

231
00:14:05,616 --> 00:14:06,575
That's right.

232
00:14:07,743 --> 00:14:08,994
Sir?

233
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:11,830
We really do understand how you feel.

234
00:14:11,914 --> 00:14:14,500
Would you like some help moving?

235
00:14:14,583 --> 00:14:19,463
We just need a moment, no,
a minute to check your luggage and--

236
00:14:19,546 --> 00:14:22,091
-All right, fine! You're so annoying.
-Thank you.

237
00:14:22,174 --> 00:14:25,219
-Thank goodness.
-Thank you very much.

238
00:14:25,302 --> 00:14:27,763
Please, go ahead.

239
00:14:28,973 --> 00:14:31,141
Thank you very much.

240
00:14:36,146 --> 00:14:37,523
Passport, please.

241
00:14:47,157 --> 00:14:49,451
-Go ahead.
-I'll check your luggage here.

242
00:14:59,128 --> 00:15:00,087
Thank you.

243
00:15:00,170 --> 00:15:01,797
Satoru Soma, right?

244
00:15:02,798 --> 00:15:03,674
What is your profession?

245
00:15:05,426 --> 00:15:09,596
Trading. I handle
infrastructure projects overseas.

246
00:15:10,431 --> 00:15:13,142
-That sounds like a respectable job.
-Doesn't it?

247
00:15:27,448 --> 00:15:30,701
-Something wrong?
-Oh, no…

248
00:15:33,037 --> 00:15:34,371
Do you have a moment?

249
00:15:39,752 --> 00:15:40,627
Mr. Soma.

250
00:15:42,629 --> 00:15:44,214
Regarding this item in your luggage…

251
00:15:59,229 --> 00:16:02,649
Sorry to keep you waiting.
How are things on the Immigration side?

252
00:16:03,484 --> 00:16:06,653
-No particular issues.
-Customs has no issues either then.

253
00:16:07,404 --> 00:16:08,238
‎Huh?

254
00:16:18,999 --> 00:16:20,209
Please, go ahead.

255
00:16:27,007 --> 00:16:28,258
What was that about?

256
00:16:28,842 --> 00:16:30,719
Was there a problem with that passenger?

257
00:16:31,553 --> 00:16:34,598
I can't say. That's Customs information.

258
00:16:34,681 --> 00:16:37,434
Wait, now Customs is doing it too?

259
00:16:37,518 --> 00:16:39,728
Didn't you say we should
share information?

260
00:16:41,897 --> 00:16:46,026
Then you tell me about that woman earlier.

261
00:16:47,444 --> 00:16:50,030
It feels like both Immigration
and Customs are so secretive.

262
00:16:50,989 --> 00:16:52,282
And the police too.

263
00:16:56,328 --> 00:16:58,664
Like I said, the flight isn't taking off!

264
00:16:59,498 --> 00:17:03,627
Can't you negotiate with them and somehow
push back tomorrow's meeting?

265
00:17:04,837 --> 00:17:05,796
Yes.

266
00:17:06,755 --> 00:17:08,590
I don't know yet.

267
00:17:11,385 --> 00:17:13,637
Thirty minutes left…

268
00:17:14,346 --> 00:17:16,014
I hope nothing happens.

269
00:17:16,098 --> 00:17:17,307
‎TIME TILL DETONATION: 30 MINUTES

270
00:17:17,391 --> 00:17:18,976
Um…

271
00:17:19,977 --> 00:17:24,523
Why was tonight's flight to Rome
targeted in the first place?

272
00:17:27,109 --> 00:17:28,235
Don't ask me.

273
00:17:28,318 --> 00:17:30,362
I was wondering about that too.

274
00:17:30,445 --> 00:17:35,784
If the perpetrator's goal were political,
there would usually be a clear message.

275
00:17:35,868 --> 00:17:38,203
It doesn't feel like that.

276
00:17:38,287 --> 00:17:42,457
Alternatively, if it were for money,
why not say there's a bomb in the airport?

277
00:17:42,541 --> 00:17:44,668
A wider-scale threat
would be more effective.

278
00:17:44,751 --> 00:17:46,128
It's strange.

279
00:17:47,087 --> 00:17:48,088
I see.

280
00:17:49,590 --> 00:17:54,303
I assumed there was some
significance to this specific airplane.

281
00:17:54,887 --> 00:17:56,430
-Significance?
-Yes.

282
00:17:56,513 --> 00:17:58,682
Though I don't know what it is yet.

283
00:17:58,765 --> 00:18:00,142
That's interesting.

284
00:18:01,018 --> 00:18:02,477
Even facing the same event,

285
00:18:02,561 --> 00:18:06,815
Hayami looks at the people
while Mori looks at the objects.

286
00:18:06,899 --> 00:18:08,859
The difference between
Immigration and Customs.

287
00:18:08,942 --> 00:18:11,653
No, no, we think about people too.

288
00:18:12,738 --> 00:18:14,823
Mori is just very unique.

289
00:18:16,408 --> 00:18:19,661
Why this specific plane, huh…

290
00:18:19,745 --> 00:18:21,872
FLIGHT NAMES

291
00:18:21,955 --> 00:18:23,040
Mr. Fukasawa.

292
00:18:25,292 --> 00:18:26,752
Hello, everyone.

293
00:18:28,337 --> 00:18:29,171
Sit down, sit down.

294
00:18:33,759 --> 00:18:34,968
What's the situation?

295
00:18:38,138 --> 00:18:40,265
No bomb has been found.

296
00:18:44,269 --> 00:18:46,230
Really?

297
00:18:48,523 --> 00:18:51,610
It's just like the incident
five years ago.

298
00:18:52,486 --> 00:18:53,320
Five years ago?

299
00:18:55,239 --> 00:18:59,701
A call came into this airport claiming
a bomb was planted on a certain flight.

300
00:19:01,161 --> 00:19:04,665
-What happened?
-The flights that day were canceled.

301
00:19:05,499 --> 00:19:07,209
No bomb was found, though.

302
00:19:07,292 --> 00:19:09,044
What a terrible prank.

303
00:19:09,127 --> 00:19:11,880
So something like that happened
before I started working here.

304
00:19:11,964 --> 00:19:13,257
I didn't even know,

305
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:17,094
-and I know everything!
-To prevent copycats,

306
00:19:18,512 --> 00:19:20,097
few people knew about that case.

307
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:22,891
It really is similar to this case.

308
00:19:24,184 --> 00:19:25,644
Could it be a coincidence?

309
00:19:30,357 --> 00:19:31,733
Yes, this is Gate 24.

310
00:19:32,859 --> 00:19:34,194
Oh, yes.

311
00:19:34,278 --> 00:19:35,195
-Open the door!
-Iuchi?

312
00:19:35,279 --> 00:19:36,530
Open the door!

313
00:19:36,613 --> 00:19:37,906
I'm coming! Come in.

314
00:19:37,990 --> 00:19:40,534
-What's wrong?
-Do you know where that couple went?

315
00:19:40,617 --> 00:19:43,203
-The couple?
-Did something happen?

316
00:19:43,287 --> 00:19:45,247
Um, that was ground staff.

317
00:19:45,330 --> 00:19:46,748
Several passengers who passed through

318
00:19:46,832 --> 00:19:48,875
the booth earlier
haven't arrived at the hotel yet.

319
00:19:49,876 --> 00:19:54,464
Sakura Nakae, Satoru Soma,
and Mr. Josef and Mrs. Luisa Meyer.

320
00:19:54,548 --> 00:19:55,590
That's it, that couple.

321
00:19:55,674 --> 00:19:56,925
Why those four?

322
00:19:57,009 --> 00:19:59,511
This is really bad, isn't it?

323
00:19:59,594 --> 00:20:00,721
There's barely any time left.

324
00:20:03,849 --> 00:20:07,936
<i>A suspicious object has been</i>
<i>discovered inside the airport.</i>

325
00:20:08,020 --> 00:20:11,106
Over there, that wasn't there
during the day.

326
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:14,443
North hallway beside the mall area!

327
00:20:15,068 --> 00:20:17,279
Suspicious object found.

328
00:20:17,904 --> 00:20:20,115
-It was real after all?
-I repeat.

329
00:20:20,198 --> 00:20:22,909
Suspicious object found.
Currently examining it.

330
00:20:22,993 --> 00:20:24,953
-Roger.
-<i>Update from the scene.</i>

331
00:20:25,037 --> 00:20:25,912
Yes.

332
00:20:25,996 --> 00:20:26,872
‎MALL AREA

333
00:20:26,955 --> 00:20:29,249
<i>The suspicious object is a hard case,</i>

334
00:20:29,333 --> 00:20:33,211
<i>color is black, plastic handle,</i>
<i>currently on its side.</i>

335
00:20:33,295 --> 00:20:36,256
No, you all can't hear this.

336
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:37,591
-Hey, let's go.
-Okay!

337
00:20:40,177 --> 00:20:41,219
Mori?

338
00:20:46,266 --> 00:20:47,142
TOKYO POLICE - KEEP OUT

339
00:20:53,106 --> 00:20:55,400
-Where is it?
-Around that pole?

340
00:20:55,484 --> 00:20:57,194
‎Hello.

341
00:20:58,236 --> 00:20:59,905
-That girl…
-Wait!

342
00:20:59,988 --> 00:21:00,947
Wait, Machi!

343
00:21:01,031 --> 00:21:03,492
Hey, what are you doing? Get back!

344
00:21:05,577 --> 00:21:06,912
It's almost time.

345
00:21:10,999 --> 00:21:13,710
What? Um…

346
00:21:13,794 --> 00:21:16,088
-That's, um…
-You can't be here.

347
00:21:17,172 --> 00:21:18,840
-Mori!
-Ten seconds left.

348
00:21:21,218 --> 00:21:23,929
That's Soma's suitcase.

349
00:21:24,763 --> 00:21:27,224
I checked the contents
at the gate earlier.

350
00:21:31,019 --> 00:21:32,104
Get down!

351
00:21:38,985 --> 00:21:40,320
MPD - KEEP OUT

352
00:21:41,154 --> 00:21:42,406
Huh?

353
00:21:45,325 --> 00:21:47,661
-The bomb…
-Yes?

354
00:21:49,246 --> 00:21:50,497
is not in there.

355
00:21:51,498 --> 00:21:52,874
-What?
-Right?

356
00:21:52,958 --> 00:21:53,917
Yes.

357
00:21:55,919 --> 00:21:59,840
-But why was it in a place like that?
-Excuse me, excuse me.

358
00:21:59,923 --> 00:22:02,175
Where have you all been?

359
00:22:02,259 --> 00:22:04,636
Oh, Josef.

360
00:22:04,719 --> 00:22:06,555
Perfect timing.

361
00:22:06,638 --> 00:22:09,975
He said he lost his bag,
so we were helping him look for it.

362
00:22:11,476 --> 00:22:13,270
Ah, that's mine!

363
00:22:14,062 --> 00:22:19,109
-Hey, wait, wait!
-Stop! It's dangerous!

364
00:22:19,192 --> 00:22:20,068
‎ARRIVALS LOBBY

365
00:22:20,152 --> 00:22:22,946
It appears the passenger
was a victim of theft.

366
00:22:23,029 --> 00:22:25,532
-Who is this person?
-We're still investigating.

367
00:22:25,615 --> 00:22:29,494
But they don't appear clearly
in other footage either.

368
00:22:33,290 --> 00:22:37,252
In the end, there was no bomb anywhere.

369
00:22:37,335 --> 00:22:39,713
Yes. No contact from
the perpetrator either.

370
00:22:39,796 --> 00:22:42,841
The police suspect
it was a malicious prank.

371
00:22:42,924 --> 00:22:45,093
Whose fault is this, damn it?!

372
00:22:48,930 --> 00:22:52,350
I saw a lot of police officers
out there earlier.

373
00:22:52,434 --> 00:22:54,394
That was, well…

374
00:22:54,477 --> 00:22:56,897
Was there a bomb scare or something?

375
00:22:58,023 --> 00:23:00,108
Ah, my apologies.

376
00:23:00,734 --> 00:23:03,653
You all just look so tense.

377
00:23:03,737 --> 00:23:06,281
No, no, there's no need to worry.

378
00:23:06,364 --> 00:23:08,867
But still, you're as sharp as ever.

379
00:23:08,950 --> 00:23:11,119
A bomb scare?

380
00:23:11,703 --> 00:23:13,622
It's probably just a prank by someone.

381
00:23:14,873 --> 00:23:16,333
Why do you think it was a prank?

382
00:23:17,292 --> 00:23:18,126
Huh?

383
00:23:18,210 --> 00:23:20,629
I was just guessing.

384
00:23:20,712 --> 00:23:23,632
More importantly,
catch the criminal, quickly!

385
00:23:23,715 --> 00:23:27,719
We'd like to ask you some details.
Would you all mind joining as well?

386
00:23:27,802 --> 00:23:28,970
Sure.

387
00:23:29,054 --> 00:23:31,765
Well then, we'll see you later.

388
00:23:38,647 --> 00:23:39,522
Iuchi.

389
00:23:41,608 --> 00:23:45,070
Earlier, you told Josef
he was as sharp as ever, right?

390
00:23:45,153 --> 00:23:47,989
I was curious about that too.
What did you mean by that?

391
00:23:49,157 --> 00:23:51,201
What were the police investigating?

392
00:23:52,410 --> 00:23:54,537
Who exactly is Josef?

393
00:23:58,208 --> 00:23:59,709
Um…

394
00:24:04,381 --> 00:24:08,009
This badge was in the Meyers' luggage.

395
00:24:08,093 --> 00:24:12,639
It's awarded to distinguished personnel
in the Ordania Police Department, right?

396
00:24:13,139 --> 00:24:15,767
<i>And for high-ranking officials, no less.</i>

397
00:24:16,351 --> 00:24:17,560
Is this supposed to be a badge?

398
00:24:18,478 --> 00:24:21,564
Mori, you really know
everything, don't you?

399
00:24:21,648 --> 00:24:23,108
Oh, no, it was just by chance.

400
00:24:23,191 --> 00:24:24,359
Is that really something
you just happen to know?

401
00:24:24,442 --> 00:24:28,321
So, Josef is a former high-ranking officer
of the Ordania Police?

402
00:24:32,075 --> 00:24:33,827
-Oh, iced coffee.
-No, it's hot.

403
00:24:34,869 --> 00:24:37,205
Well, we've collaborated
with him a few times

404
00:24:37,289 --> 00:24:39,124
<i>on international crime investigations.</i>

405
00:24:39,207 --> 00:24:41,584
<i>When we heard he was among</i>
<i>the passengers today,</i>

406
00:24:41,668 --> 00:24:44,170
we were instructed from above
to treat him with utmost respect.

407
00:24:44,796 --> 00:24:47,340
What? So it was just VIP treatment?

408
00:24:47,424 --> 00:24:49,926
-Huh?
-No, no, VIP treatment is important.

409
00:24:50,010 --> 00:24:51,344
I see.

410
00:24:52,012 --> 00:24:54,723
So that's why it was kept secret.

411
00:24:54,806 --> 00:24:57,392
By the way, both Immigration
and Customs are hiding something.

412
00:24:58,059 --> 00:25:01,062
That's right. It's time you told us!

413
00:25:02,314 --> 00:25:03,565
Did something happen?

414
00:25:06,443 --> 00:25:07,694
Okay…

415
00:25:09,362 --> 00:25:11,072
About Sakura Nakae…

416
00:25:11,740 --> 00:25:16,077
She has a past record
of being detained by foreign authorities.

417
00:25:16,161 --> 00:25:18,580
<i>It seems she worked a side job</i>
<i>in nightlife entertainment.</i>

418
00:25:18,663 --> 00:25:22,500
<i>However, the severity was low, and it is</i>
<i>unrelated to her current situation.</i>

419
00:25:22,584 --> 00:25:26,546
Above all, since it concerns her privacy,

420
00:25:26,629 --> 00:25:29,049
I believed it shouldn't
be shared recklessly.

421
00:25:29,632 --> 00:25:32,218
I see. That's true.

422
00:25:32,302 --> 00:25:34,846
It might not be something
to go around telling people.

423
00:25:34,929 --> 00:25:38,224
As expected of you, Mr. Hayami.
I thought as much.

424
00:25:39,059 --> 00:25:41,186
And what about Customs?

425
00:25:44,022 --> 00:25:46,232
Regarding Soma, inside his luggage…

426
00:25:49,027 --> 00:25:51,029
-there was a magazine.
-A magazine?

427
00:25:52,072 --> 00:25:54,783
An adult magazine. Uncensored.

428
00:25:58,912 --> 00:26:03,124
So that means… In other words…

429
00:26:03,208 --> 00:26:04,834
A porno-mag, right?

430
00:26:06,044 --> 00:26:09,923
It might be fine overseas, but it's not
allowed to be brought into Japan.

431
00:26:10,590 --> 00:26:14,135
<i>So that's why he was reluctant</i>
<i>to go through processing!</i>

432
00:26:14,219 --> 00:26:16,304
The magazine was confiscated.

433
00:26:16,388 --> 00:26:20,558
But since this also
concerned a passenger's privacy…

434
00:26:21,309 --> 00:26:22,894
So that's what it was.

435
00:26:22,977 --> 00:26:27,982
In the end, everyone was acting
out of consideration for the passengers.

436
00:26:28,066 --> 00:26:33,530
With different positions
and responsibilities, sharing information

437
00:26:34,114 --> 00:26:35,573
can be quite challenging.

438
00:26:46,418 --> 00:26:47,877
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

439
00:26:48,420 --> 00:26:49,295
Thank you very much.

440
00:26:50,338 --> 00:26:53,800
Counselor, the task force is dissolved.

441
00:26:53,883 --> 00:26:56,302
The passengers from that flight
will be rebooked

442
00:26:56,386 --> 00:26:58,221
on an early morning temporary flight.

443
00:26:59,889 --> 00:27:01,057
Still working on something?

444
00:27:01,141 --> 00:27:05,311
Five years ago, there was
a similar commotion, wasn't there?

445
00:27:06,646 --> 00:27:08,690
That was a real nuisance.

446
00:27:09,732 --> 00:27:10,608
What about it?

447
00:27:12,777 --> 00:27:15,071
Do you have detailed records?

448
00:27:24,414 --> 00:27:26,624
This way, please.
We will take you to the hotel.

449
00:27:28,209 --> 00:27:29,461
May I go as well?

450
00:27:30,295 --> 00:27:31,921
Yes, and Soma, if you'd like.

451
00:27:32,005 --> 00:27:34,757
Of course! I went through a nightmare.

452
00:27:35,383 --> 00:27:37,886
Well, I'll let it slide this time.

453
00:27:38,887 --> 00:27:41,973
Actually, I just got good news.

454
00:27:42,056 --> 00:27:44,976
Today's business meeting
has been postponed.

455
00:27:46,144 --> 00:27:49,731
A lot happened,
but all's well that ends well.

456
00:27:53,776 --> 00:27:54,694
Thank you.

457
00:27:57,238 --> 00:27:59,699
Nakatsuka, let's load the luggage.

458
00:28:00,783 --> 00:28:01,910
I'll take this for you.

459
00:28:04,120 --> 00:28:05,705
Hey, what are you doing?

460
00:28:05,788 --> 00:28:07,582
-I'm very sorry!
-Sorry.

461
00:28:19,594 --> 00:28:22,138
-Is this everything?
-Yes. Thank you very much.

462
00:28:23,097 --> 00:28:26,476
-Are you sure? Is there any other…
-It's fine now, really.

463
00:28:27,769 --> 00:28:29,896
-Okay.
-Pardon us.

464
00:28:31,731 --> 00:28:33,483
Let me help you.

465
00:28:33,566 --> 00:28:36,611
Oh, I'm good, thank you. I'm very good.

466
00:28:50,959 --> 00:28:52,001
Matsuyama,

467
00:28:52,961 --> 00:28:55,046
what were you looking for earlier?

468
00:28:55,129 --> 00:28:57,465
Ah, Nakae's chalk. I felt like

469
00:28:57,549 --> 00:28:59,676
there were fewer boxes
than when I saw them at the booth.

470
00:29:00,468 --> 00:29:01,427
Fewer?

471
00:29:02,095 --> 00:29:04,973
That's what I thought,
but she said it was fine.

472
00:29:06,057 --> 00:29:10,186
Then there shouldn't be a problem.
That concludes our work for today.

473
00:29:10,270 --> 00:29:14,190
Finally heading home.
Ah, what a crazy day.

474
00:29:52,061 --> 00:29:55,315
-Hey, everybody.
-Hello.

475
00:29:55,398 --> 00:30:00,153
The Meyers arrived safely
at the airport from the hotel.

476
00:30:00,236 --> 00:30:03,406
That ends our VIP duty.

477
00:30:03,489 --> 00:30:06,075
We appreciate your cooperation,
more or less.

478
00:30:08,202 --> 00:30:10,371
He actually called it VIP duty…

479
00:30:10,455 --> 00:30:12,624
And he doesn't sound thankful at all.

480
00:30:16,127 --> 00:30:17,503
What are you looking at?

481
00:30:18,254 --> 00:30:21,966
There's something that
has been bugging me.

482
00:30:27,388 --> 00:30:29,557
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

483
00:30:29,641 --> 00:30:31,517
Everyone got some good sleep?

484
00:30:31,601 --> 00:30:33,603
Yes, somehow.

485
00:30:34,479 --> 00:30:37,106
So in the end, no bomb was found.

486
00:30:37,190 --> 00:30:38,816
It seems it was a prank,

487
00:30:40,109 --> 00:30:42,820
almost the same as five years ago.

488
00:30:44,030 --> 00:30:45,239
Um…

489
00:30:47,283 --> 00:30:50,495
What do you mean by "almost the same"?

490
00:30:51,621 --> 00:30:54,040
Was the targeted flight the same as well?

491
00:30:54,123 --> 00:30:55,041
No, not that similar.

492
00:30:56,417 --> 00:30:59,837
This time it was bound for Rome,
but five years ago,

493
00:30:59,921 --> 00:31:04,968
the culprit specified
a flight to Oslo, Norway.

494
00:31:05,051 --> 00:31:06,177
Norway?

495
00:31:06,886 --> 00:31:11,849
The country where the Meyers' daughter
performs music.

496
00:31:11,933 --> 00:31:13,768
<i>Right. Yes, that's right!</i>

497
00:31:17,480 --> 00:31:18,314
What's wrong?

498
00:31:19,649 --> 00:31:25,029
Oh, it's just, Sakura Nakae's
past side job was also in Norway.

499
00:31:25,113 --> 00:31:27,699
<i>-And it was five years ago.</i>
<i>-Nakae too?</i>

500
00:31:27,782 --> 00:31:31,619
Furthermore, Soma's passport travel
history included Norway.

501
00:31:31,703 --> 00:31:32,954
<i>Five years ago as well.</i>

502
00:31:33,496 --> 00:31:35,748
All three of them, in the same country
at the same time…

503
00:31:36,666 --> 00:31:39,168
-Could it be a coincidence?
-Wait a second.

504
00:31:40,336 --> 00:31:43,673
The Meyers' daughter already passed away.

505
00:31:43,756 --> 00:31:44,841
Since when?

506
00:31:46,009 --> 00:31:47,176
Five years ago.

507
00:31:50,471 --> 00:31:55,351
<i>Wait, wait! Does that mean everything</i>
<i>connects back to Norway five years ago?</i>

508
00:31:55,435 --> 00:31:56,894
<i>-The bomb threat,</i>
-Emma…

509
00:31:56,978 --> 00:31:59,397
<i>Sakura Nakae, Soma,</i>

510
00:32:00,356 --> 00:32:01,816
and the Meyers' daughter?

511
00:32:04,485 --> 00:32:06,070
Um…

512
00:32:09,323 --> 00:32:11,951
May I say something as well?

513
00:32:13,953 --> 00:32:17,248
Last night, when we were seeing off
Josef to the hotel,

514
00:32:17,331 --> 00:32:19,083
something felt off to me.

515
00:32:19,917 --> 00:32:22,879
So, I rewatched the footage…

516
00:32:22,962 --> 00:32:23,796
CUSTOMS BOOTH A CAMERA

517
00:32:23,880 --> 00:32:27,508
…and several parts
of the wheelchair were missing.

518
00:32:30,136 --> 00:32:31,679
Pardon us.

519
00:32:33,306 --> 00:32:36,809
-Let me help you.
-Oh, I'm good, thank you. I'm very good.

520
00:32:36,893 --> 00:32:38,394
Parts of the wheelchair?

521
00:32:39,062 --> 00:32:43,524
Yes. And Luisa's pendant
had changed as well.

522
00:32:44,484 --> 00:32:46,944
And you said it earlier too, Matsuyama,

523
00:32:47,028 --> 00:32:48,988
about Sakura Nakae's luggage.

524
00:32:49,072 --> 00:32:52,200
Ah, I felt like the number
of chalk boxes had decreased.

525
00:32:53,159 --> 00:32:57,997
So I extracted the missing items
and assembled them…

526
00:33:02,168 --> 00:33:03,169
and got this.

527
00:33:13,262 --> 00:33:14,347
You dropped this.

528
00:33:22,188 --> 00:33:23,731
Will you come with us?

529
00:33:25,316 --> 00:33:26,400
‎Stand up.

530
00:33:31,280 --> 00:33:33,533
-This is…
-Uh…

531
00:33:34,325 --> 00:33:35,243
What is it?

532
00:33:36,077 --> 00:33:37,453
A gun. It's a gun.

533
00:33:38,704 --> 00:33:41,749
It has a structure close
to a small single-shot pistol.

534
00:33:41,833 --> 00:33:44,961
<i>If so, the bullet</i>
<i>was likely Luisa's pendant.</i>

535
00:33:45,044 --> 00:33:50,383
<i>The gunpowder needed to fire it</i>
<i>was probably mixed into Sakura's chalk.</i>

536
00:34:00,726 --> 00:34:01,561
Get on the phone.

537
00:34:01,644 --> 00:34:02,937
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

538
00:34:05,523 --> 00:34:06,941
-Just this way.
-Thank you.

539
00:34:09,861 --> 00:34:11,028
Wheelchair located!

540
00:34:12,321 --> 00:34:15,408
-Hey, what is this about?
-Shut up.

541
00:34:20,872 --> 00:34:23,457
Do you recognize this girl?

542
00:34:23,541 --> 00:34:26,794
I just got information
from Counselor Sugihara.

543
00:34:26,878 --> 00:34:29,881
<i>The passenger manifest</i>
<i>for the targeted flight</i>

544
00:34:29,964 --> 00:34:32,717
<i>during the bomb scare</i>
<i>five years ago contained</i>

545
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:34,760
<i>Emma and Soma.</i>

546
00:34:35,344 --> 00:34:40,516
We are currently investigating
what kind of connection there could be.

547
00:34:42,518 --> 00:34:43,603
<i>I met Emma</i>

548
00:34:45,354 --> 00:34:47,064
<i>on a music website.</i>

549
00:34:47,773 --> 00:34:49,483
<i>At first, I was just a fan.</i>

550
00:34:50,234 --> 00:34:51,903
<i>But before I knew it,</i>

551
00:34:52,737 --> 00:34:55,489
we started
contacting each other every day.

552
00:34:57,408 --> 00:34:59,493
That wasn't all, was it?

553
00:35:00,244 --> 00:35:03,497
Sakura truly loved her
from the bottom of her heart.

554
00:35:06,626 --> 00:35:07,793
And Emma

555
00:35:09,337 --> 00:35:10,421
loved her too.

556
00:35:12,131 --> 00:35:14,300
Emma!

557
00:35:15,176 --> 00:35:17,720
<i>Emma was aiming for an international</i>
<i>competition held in Norway.</i>

558
00:35:19,305 --> 00:35:20,806
<i>Winning it</i>

559
00:35:20,890 --> 00:35:22,808
<i>would pave her path</i>
<i>to a prestigious orchestra.</i>

560
00:35:22,892 --> 00:35:24,143
I'm good. How was your flight?

561
00:35:27,813 --> 00:35:30,066
It was the competition
Emma staked her life on.

562
00:35:31,359 --> 00:35:33,027
<i>The day before,</i>

563
00:35:33,110 --> 00:35:36,072
<i>Emma was supposed to transfer</i>
<i>at this airport and head to Norway.</i>

564
00:35:36,155 --> 00:35:37,990
We are currently unable
to board your flight.

565
00:35:38,074 --> 00:35:40,534
But I checked this morning.

566
00:35:40,618 --> 00:35:43,204
-It said it was fine.
-I'm so sorry.

567
00:35:43,829 --> 00:35:44,914
<i>But suddenly,</i>

568
00:35:46,207 --> 00:35:47,917
<i>her flight was canceled.</i>

569
00:35:49,502 --> 00:35:50,336
<i>In the end,</i>

570
00:35:51,712 --> 00:35:53,214
the rescheduled flight was too late.

571
00:35:56,259 --> 00:35:57,760
<i>That wasn't all.</i>

572
00:35:59,637 --> 00:36:01,973
<i>Her precious violin</i>
<i>was stolen at the airport too.</i>

573
00:36:03,891 --> 00:36:07,478
<i>In total shock, Emma was in a daze.</i>

574
00:36:13,276 --> 00:36:14,151
And?

575
00:36:15,194 --> 00:36:16,279
So what?

576
00:36:17,530 --> 00:36:20,616
I feel bad for her,
but what does that have to do with me?

577
00:36:21,409 --> 00:36:23,286
-Bastard...
-Everyone, this way!

578
00:36:24,870 --> 00:36:25,705
‎Go.

579
00:36:34,088 --> 00:36:36,173
-Going there now.
-Roger that.

580
00:36:44,849 --> 00:36:45,891
Found them!

581
00:36:47,393 --> 00:36:49,270
K Area, near the VIP entrance.

582
00:36:52,898 --> 00:36:54,025
Nothing to do with you?

583
00:36:55,776 --> 00:36:58,029
Did you say it has nothing to do with you?

584
00:36:58,112 --> 00:37:01,699
After losing Emma, I went to Norway.

585
00:37:02,825 --> 00:37:05,786
I at least wanted to see
the country she longed for.

586
00:37:06,996 --> 00:37:08,331
I worked in nightlife there too.

587
00:37:09,665 --> 00:37:12,418
Man, that was a close call, seriously.

588
00:37:12,501 --> 00:37:13,961
Did something happen?

589
00:37:14,045 --> 00:37:18,382
Six months ago, I had a huge
business meeting in this country,

590
00:37:18,466 --> 00:37:19,842
but I overslept.

591
00:37:19,925 --> 00:37:22,428
When I woke up,
the plane was about to depart.

592
00:37:22,511 --> 00:37:25,639
-What? That must have been awful.
-Yes.

593
00:37:25,723 --> 00:37:27,850
Normally, it would be game over.

594
00:37:27,933 --> 00:37:30,269
But I'm different.

595
00:37:30,353 --> 00:37:32,438
I made a quick phone call to the airport.

596
00:37:32,521 --> 00:37:34,315
-A phone call?
-Yes.

597
00:37:34,398 --> 00:37:38,986
A magic phone call.
With just one call, I delayed the flight.

598
00:37:39,987 --> 00:37:43,908
Thanks to that, I made it to the plane
and barely made the meeting.

599
00:37:44,909 --> 00:37:47,536
That was brilliant of me, huh?

600
00:37:50,706 --> 00:37:53,000
I wanted you to experience
the exact same thing.

601
00:37:55,127 --> 00:37:56,879
I wanted your flight delayed

602
00:37:58,839 --> 00:38:00,841
so you would lose what matters most.

603
00:38:10,476 --> 00:38:13,687
<i>This is the Information Center</i>
<i>of Kanto International Airport.</i>

604
00:38:15,064 --> 00:38:18,526
A bomb has been planted on the flight
bound for Rome International Airport.

605
00:38:23,989 --> 00:38:26,534
Could it be, my bag too?

606
00:38:28,244 --> 00:38:29,745
Just like Emma.

607
00:38:29,829 --> 00:38:32,206
Like I said, the flight isn't taking off!

608
00:38:33,707 --> 00:38:37,420
Can't you negotiate with them and somehow
push back tomorrow's meeting?

609
00:38:38,546 --> 00:38:39,380
Yes.

610
00:38:39,964 --> 00:38:42,466
I don't know yet.

611
00:38:46,554 --> 00:38:47,680
Stop!

612
00:38:49,473 --> 00:38:50,391
Stop.

613
00:38:51,142 --> 00:38:52,810
Shoot him!

614
00:38:57,982 --> 00:38:59,442
‎I can't do it.

615
00:39:01,902 --> 00:39:02,945
Um…

616
00:39:03,028 --> 00:39:04,780
-Mori, stop!
-Stop!

617
00:39:04,864 --> 00:39:06,866
W-wait! It's my fault!

618
00:39:06,949 --> 00:39:08,742
I was the one
who stopped the plane back then!

619
00:39:08,826 --> 00:39:11,579
But I didn't think
it would turn out like that!

620
00:39:14,290 --> 00:39:15,958
Give Emma back.

621
00:39:26,302 --> 00:39:27,553
Um…

622
00:39:29,096 --> 00:39:32,641
This is the firing pin.
Without this, it won't fire.

623
00:39:43,068 --> 00:39:45,613
Josef, you must already know.

624
00:39:48,073 --> 00:39:52,411
When I assembled it,
I realized the firing pin was missing.

625
00:39:53,287 --> 00:39:55,539
-But…
-All we wanted from this man

626
00:39:55,623 --> 00:39:57,374
was an apology to Emma.

627
00:40:00,586 --> 00:40:01,712
Where was it?

628
00:40:02,796 --> 00:40:04,924
At Gate 24.

629
00:40:05,007 --> 00:40:06,175
What?

630
00:40:10,387 --> 00:40:11,639
What's wrong with you?

631
00:40:22,399 --> 00:40:23,651
That was it?

632
00:40:37,206 --> 00:40:40,125
‎I think Emma probably stopped us

633
00:40:40,209 --> 00:40:43,796
‎-from doing something foolish.
‎-That's right.

634
00:41:15,286 --> 00:41:17,788
I could have died!

635
00:41:17,871 --> 00:41:20,749
Because your airport security was lacking!

636
00:41:22,960 --> 00:41:23,919
Hey!

637
00:41:26,714 --> 00:41:30,301
Excuse me. I am Sugihara.

638
00:41:31,510 --> 00:41:34,972
We are truly sorry for the trouble caused.

639
00:41:35,055 --> 00:41:39,560
Absolutely! In the end, I couldn't
even attend my important meeting.

640
00:41:40,769 --> 00:41:44,315
I'm going to claim damages for this.

641
00:41:44,398 --> 00:41:46,650
Is that so? Against whom?

642
00:41:47,276 --> 00:41:48,193
Huh?

643
00:41:48,277 --> 00:41:51,030
The bomb threat five years ago,

644
00:41:51,113 --> 00:41:54,241
voiceprint analysis and call records
from that time confirmed

645
00:41:55,409 --> 00:41:59,246
it was your doing, Mr. Soma.

646
00:42:01,540 --> 00:42:03,834
The statute of limitations
for this matter has not expired yet.

647
00:42:04,710 --> 00:42:07,713
You may face prosecution
for fraudulent obstruction of business

648
00:42:07,796 --> 00:42:10,549
and attempted extortion.

649
00:42:10,633 --> 00:42:11,842
Um…

650
00:42:11,925 --> 00:42:16,805
In addition, the airport plans to file
a claim for damages against you.

651
00:42:16,889 --> 00:42:19,600
At least in the hundreds
of millions of yen.

652
00:42:19,683 --> 00:42:23,729
That is the gravity of what you did.

653
00:42:32,655 --> 00:42:33,864
A BOOTH - B BOOTH - PLANTS AND ANIMALS
CUSTOMS - MOBILE PERSONNEL

654
00:42:33,947 --> 00:42:35,115
SCHEDULED FLIGHTS

655
00:42:35,199 --> 00:42:36,325
BRISBANE - PANAMA CITY
SHANGHAI - BARCELONA

656
00:42:39,370 --> 00:42:40,954
Is something wrong?

657
00:42:42,081 --> 00:42:43,207
I must confess.

658
00:42:43,290 --> 00:42:47,002
I missed the weapons being brought in.

659
00:42:47,670 --> 00:42:49,797
If we're talking about that,
then so did I.

660
00:42:49,880 --> 00:42:53,342
Me too. It's really frustrating.

661
00:42:53,425 --> 00:42:55,803
But asking anyone to spot that
would be impossible, right?

662
00:42:55,886 --> 00:42:57,346
It couldn't be helped.

663
00:42:57,930 --> 00:43:00,391
It was impossible. It couldn't be helped.

664
00:43:02,101 --> 00:43:04,019
Is it really okay to excuse it like that?

665
00:43:04,978 --> 00:43:06,605
You didn't spot it either.

666
00:43:06,689 --> 00:43:09,024
No, like I said, I--

667
00:43:09,108 --> 00:43:12,778
-Now, now, both of you!
-Fighting again?

668
00:43:14,238 --> 00:43:15,698
Counselor Sugihara.

669
00:43:15,781 --> 00:43:19,034
Thank you so much
for your hard work, everyone.

670
00:43:19,118 --> 00:43:23,497
But in the future, please be mindful
of what our team's name means.

671
00:43:24,248 --> 00:43:26,917
-Our team's name?
-Gate 24?

672
00:43:27,000 --> 00:43:29,795
Come to think of it,
I've wondered for a while.

673
00:43:29,878 --> 00:43:32,423
What does 24 mean?

674
00:43:32,506 --> 00:43:36,885
Does it mean a gate that responds
to any situation 24 hours a day?

675
00:43:38,512 --> 00:43:40,764
That was certainly true this time.

676
00:43:41,765 --> 00:43:43,225
But there is another meaning.

677
00:43:44,518 --> 00:43:45,644
Two times four.

678
00:43:46,353 --> 00:43:48,063
Two times four?

679
00:43:48,147 --> 00:43:49,440
Eight?

680
00:43:49,523 --> 00:43:51,024
No, that's not it.

681
00:43:51,108 --> 00:43:56,697
It means evaluating both people
and objects through the four perspectives

682
00:43:56,780 --> 00:43:59,283
of Immigration, Customs,
Quarantine, and Police.

683
00:43:59,366 --> 00:44:03,954
This team is a gathering of people
with different positions.

684
00:44:05,414 --> 00:44:06,498
However,

685
00:44:07,499 --> 00:44:10,127
precisely because each of you
has a different perspective,

686
00:44:11,128 --> 00:44:12,379
there are things only you can notice.

687
00:44:14,047 --> 00:44:18,677
That is the true strength of Gate 24.

688
00:44:19,595 --> 00:44:21,388
So, everybody,

689
00:44:22,264 --> 00:44:25,100
try to get along a little better.

690
00:44:28,103 --> 00:44:29,480
Oh my…

691
00:44:37,780 --> 00:44:41,033
PLANTS AND ANIMALS INSPECTION

692
00:44:46,246 --> 00:44:48,791
‎-<i>‎My son was kidnapped.</i>
‎-<i>‎Kidnapped…</i>

693
00:44:48,874 --> 00:44:50,709
<i>‎We lost track of an animal,</i>
<i>‎which we must monitor,</i>

694
00:44:50,792 --> 00:44:53,003
<i>‎and a child, who we must protect,</i>
<i>‎at the same time!</i>

695
00:44:53,086 --> 00:44:54,671
<i>‎I made a mistake at a critical time.</i>

696
00:44:54,755 --> 00:44:55,631
<i>‎Hayami!</i>

697
00:44:57,049 --> 00:44:59,176
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman

